---
import Policy from "../layouts/Policy.astro";
import { REMOVAL_ADDRESS } from "../lib/launch.ts";
---

<Policy title="Code of conduct">
  <p>
    The&nbsp;Rupee&nbsp;Fund is a FOSS United community initiative run by community members. We
    adopt the conduct and anti-harassment standards of the{" "}
    <a
      href="https://fossunited.org/code-of-conduct"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="inline-link">FOSS United Code of Conduct</a
    >, as reviewed on 7 September 2026, with the local rules below. Later changes to that source do
    not change this policy automatically. Where the source differs from the local rules, the local
    rules apply to the spaces of The&nbsp;Rupee&nbsp;Fund.
  </p>
  <h2>Scope and conduct</h2>
  <p>
    These standards apply to contributors, applicants, volunteers, and organisers in the spaces of
    The&nbsp;Rupee&nbsp;Fund and fund-related communications. Treat people with respect. Harassment,
    threats, discrimination, and disclosure of another person’s private information are not
    permitted.
  </p>
  <h2>Responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/people" class="inline-link">community team</a> is responsible for conduct in the spaces
    of The&nbsp;Rupee&nbsp;Fund. The Foundation contacts and event enforcement roles in the source policy
    are not assigned responsibilities in The&nbsp;Rupee&nbsp;Fund by this adoption. Foundation spaces
    remain subject to their own reporting procedures.
  </p>
  <h2>Report a concern</h2>
  <p>
    To report a concern in a space of The&nbsp;Rupee&nbsp;Fund, email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${REMOVAL_ADDRESS}`} class="inline-link">{REMOVAL_ADDRESS}</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Attribution</h2>
  <p>
    The adopted standards come from FOSS United. Its source credits the Major League Hacking
    policies under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence. This local adaptation
    uses the same <a
      href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="inline-link">licence</a
    >.
  </p>
</Policy>
